
# 🔍 Parse-Local

> Like [Parse.bot](https://parse.bot) but runs 100% on your machine.
> No API keys. No cloud. No data leaves your PC.

Give it a URL and describe what you want. Get back structured JSON.
The LLM runs locally via llama.cpp — nothing is sent anywhere.

---

## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- 8 GB RAM minimum (16 GB recommended)
- 8 GB free disk space
- GPU optional but recommended

---

## Install & Run

**Linux / macOS**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/parse-local.git
cd parse-local
chmod +x setup.sh && ./setup.sh
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m app.main
```

**Windows**
```bat
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/parse-local.git
cd parse-local
setup.bat
.venv\Scripts\activate.bat
python -m app.main
```

Open **http://localhost:8000**

> First run downloads the model (~7 GB). Subsequent starts are instant.

---

## Docker

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

---

## API

**Scrape a URL**
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/scrape/url \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com",
    "prompt": "Extract the top 10 story titles and scores"
  }'
```

**Parse raw HTML**
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/scrape/html \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "html": "<div>...</div>",
    "prompt": "Extract all product names and prices"
  }'
```

**Response**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { ... },
  "elapsed_seconds": 14.2
}
```

---

## Configuration

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```bash
N_GPU_LAYERS=-1   # -1 = all on GPU, 0 = CPU only
N_CTX=8192        # context window size
TEMPERATURE=0.1   # lower = more consistent output
PORT=8000         # server port
```

---

## GPU Setup

**NVIDIA (CUDA)**
```bash
pip uninstall llama-cpp-python -y
CMAKE_ARGS="-DGGML_CUDA=on" pip install llama-cpp-python --no-cache-dir
```

**Apple Silicon (Metal)**
```bash
pip uninstall llama-cpp-python -y
CMAKE_ARGS="-DGGML_METAL=on" pip install llama-cpp-python --no-cache-dir
```

---

## Troubleshooting

**Model download failed**
Download `Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-Q4_K_M.gguf` manually from
[bartowski/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/bartowski/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-GGUF)
and place it in the `models/` directory.

**llama-cpp-python install failed**
```bash
# Linux
sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake -y

# macOS
xcode-select --install
```
On Windows install [Visual Studio Build Tools](https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/visual-cpp-build-tools/) with C++ workload.

**Out of memory**
Set `N_CTX=4096` or `N_GPU_LAYERS=0` in your `.env` file.

**Port already in use**
```bash
PORT=8080 python -m app.main
```

